{"8f15b6d5f3": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Company Description\nWe are Olsson. We engineer and design solutions that improve the world around us. As a company, we promise to always be responsive, transparent, and focused on results – for our people, our clients, and our company.\nWe’re a people-centric firm, so it’s no surprise our greatest asset is our people. The impact this creates is an environment that encourages our people to grow and be creative with their talents. This approach builds a culture that is uniquely Olsson. It allows us to grow our people as we grow our business. This, in turn, creates a lasting impact on the world around us.\nJob Description\nOlsson's Facilities Engineering and Design Team is at the forefront of engineering innovation, providing comprehensive services for large commercial developments, healthcare facilities, laboratories, educational institutions, data centers, and military installations.\n\nOur expertise includes engineering analysis, design services, and professional consulting, ensuring top-tier quality and world class installations. We also provide building inspection and forensic investigation services.\n\nAs a member of this team, you will contribute to diverse, high-impact projects, delivering engineering solutions that make a tangible difference in communities and industries.\nThe Lead Engineer role oversees high-level project design and manages the overall design tasks within the structural group. As a Lead Engineer, you will make influential recommendations and decisions regarding advanced engineering activities and specialized client-type standards and have full technical responsibility of design assignments. This role manages the delivery of advanced project designs that provide purposeful, high-quality solutions to successfully solve engineering and design needs."}, {"h": "Primary Responsibilities", "t": "Leads large-scale project design by serving as a technical lead for complex assignments and managing the design from initial design to project completion.\nExecutes high-level analysis and review of project documents ensuring compliance with applicable standards, codes, and regulations.\nOversees and regularly monitors engineering processes and resources to maximize productivity and efficiency.\nDevelops and implements standards and guidelines for diverse engineering activities to ensure high-quality results.\nElevates the level of technical expertise within the team through technical design training and mentoring.\nSupports project management objectives by providing leadership and direction regarding organizing technical resources for key projects and utilizing resources effectively.\nCollaborates with project managers to ensure technical aspects of projects are completed on time, within budget, and meet established objectives.\nDemonstrates an elevated degree of creativity, decision-making, and responsibility for design tasks within a specific discipline."}, {"h": "You are passionate about", "t": "Working collaboratively with others.\nHaving ownership in the work you do.\nUsing your talents to positively affect communities."}, {"h": "You bring to the team", "t": "Strong communication skills.\nAbility to contribute and work well on a team.\nMaster's Degree in Structural Engineering or Civil or Architectural Engineering with a structural emphasis.\n12-20+ years of related Structural Engineering experience.\nMust be a registered professional and have at least four years of experience supervising technical personnel.\nProven track record in meeting and exceeding client expectations through technical design work.\nExcellent client service orientation.\nSolid interpersonal and decision-making skills and the ability to generate innovative and effective solutions to complex problems."}, {"h": "#LI-RS1", "t": "Additional Information\nOlsson specializes in engineering and design, client advisory services, planning, field services, and environmental. Improving the world has been our mindset from the very beginning, back when Olsson first opened for business in 1956. And it will be our mindset for years to come."}, {"h": "As an Olsson employee, you will", "t": "Receive a competitive 401(k) match\nBe empowered to build your career with tailored development paths\nHave the possibility for flexible work arrangements\nEngage in work that has a positive impact on communities\nParticipate in a wellness program promoting balanced lifestyles\nIn addition, full-time employees will receive our traditional benefits package (health care, vision, dental, paid time off, etc.) and the opportunity to participate in a bonus system that rewards performance.\nOlsson is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage qualified minority, female, veteran, and disabled candidates to apply and be considered for open positions. We do not discriminate against any applicant for employment or any employee because of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender, disability, age, military status, or other protected status.\nOlsson understands the importance of privacy and is committed to protecting job applicants’ personal information. Pursuant to the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (collectively, the “CCPA”), this notice explains Olsson’s practices regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal information for job applicants residing in California. Please read this Notice carefully to understand our privacy practices.\nFor more information about the types of information we collect and how we use it in connection with your general access and use of our website, please review our general California Privacy Notice here ."}], "k": ["project-management", "training"], "b": ["generous-pto"], "r": {"exp": 12, "edu": {"level": "master", "state": "required"}}}, "6439564e64": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Company Description\nWe are Olsson. We engineer and design solutions that improve the world around us. As a company, we promise to always be responsive, transparent, and focused on results – for our people, our clients, and our company.\nWe’re a people-centric firm, so it’s no surprise our greatest asset is our people. The impact this creates is an environment that encourages our people to grow and be creative with their talents. This approach builds a culture that is uniquely Olsson. It allows us to grow our people as we grow our business. This, in turn, creates a lasting impact on the world around us.\nJob Description\nAs a Senior Engineer on our Railroad Bridge team, you will play a key role in the planning, design, and delivery of railroad bridge and structural projects.\n\nYou will work closely with project managers, technical leaders, and clients to develop practical engineering solutions while providing technical guidance and mentorship to less experienced engineers.\n\nThis position offers the opportunity to lead technical design efforts, contribute to project success, and help deliver high-quality solutions that meet client needs and project objectives."}, {"h": "Primary Responsibilities will include", "t": "Lead the structural analysis and design of railroad bridges and related structures for a variety of transportation projects.\nPrepare and review engineering calculations, plans, specifications, and technical reports to ensure quality and accuracy.\nProvide technical direction and mentorship to junior engineers and engineering staff.\nCoordinate with multidisciplinary teams to develop innovative and practical design solutions.\nSupport project planning efforts by assisting with scope development, scheduling, budgeting, and resource coordination.\nConduct quality control reviews and ensure compliance with applicable design standards, codes, and client requirements.\nCollaborate directly with clients, contractors, railroads, and regulatory agencies throughout project development and delivery.\nAssist with business development activities, including proposal preparation, client relationship management, and identifying opportunities for future work.\nMaintain comprehensive project documentation, including design files, calculations, correspondence, and technical deliverables."}, {"h": "You are passionate about", "t": "Working collaboratively with others.\nHaving ownership in the work you do.\nUsing your talents to positively affect communities.\nMentoring and supporting the growth of developing engineers."}, {"h": "You bring to the team", "t": "Bachelor’s degree in Civil Engineering, Structural Engineering, or a related engineering field.\nMinimum of 8 years of relevant experience supporting railroad bridge and structure design projects.\nStrong knowledge of railroad bridge design principles, structural analysis, and industry standards.\nExperience leading technical design efforts and coordinating project deliverables.\nExcellent communication, collaboration, and problem-solving skills.\nProven ability to build and maintain strong client relationships.\nProfessional Engineering (P.E.) license required.\nExperience with MicroStation, RISA 3D, and Bluebeam Revu.\nValid driver’s license and a good driving history.\nWillingness to work a flexible schedule and travel as required.\n#LI-Remote"}, {"h": "#LI-AF1", "t": "Additional Information\nOlsson specializes in engineering and design, client advisory services, planning, field services, and environmental. Improving the world has been our mindset from the very beginning, back when Olsson first opened for business in 1956. And it will be our mindset for years to come."}, {"h": "As an Olsson employee, you will", "t": "Receive a competitive 401(k) match\nBe empowered to build your career with tailored development paths\nHave the possibility for flexible work arrangements\nEngage in work that has a positive impact on communities\nParticipate in a wellness program promoting balanced lifestyles\nIn addition, full-time employees will receive our traditional benefits package (health care, vision, dental, paid time off, etc.) and the opportunity to participate in a bonus system that rewards performance.\nOlsson is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage qualified minority, female, veteran, and disabled candidates to apply and be considered for open positions. We do not discriminate against any applicant for employment or any employee because of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender, disability, age, military status, or other protected status.\nOlsson understands the importance of privacy and is committed to protecting job applicants’ personal information. Pursuant to the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (collectively, the “CCPA”), this notice explains Olsson’s practices regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal information for job applicants residing in California. Please read this Notice carefully to understand our privacy practices.\nFor more information about the types of information we collect and how we use it in connection with your general access and use of our website, please review our general California Privacy Notice here ."}], "k": ["account-management", "bluebeam", "bridge-design", "budgeting", "business-development", "etabs", "fea", "microstation", "project-management", "quality-control", "scheduling", "structural-analysis", "training"], "b": ["flexible-hours", "generous-pto"], "r": {"exp": 8, "edu": {"level": "bachelor", "state": "required"}}}, "884f3573e8": {"s": [{"h": "Overview", "t": "Exercises independent judgment in evaluation, selection and use of standard techniques, and solves problems when encountered. A licensed engineer who works on a variety of projects on structural design, preparation of implementation documentation, coordination with clients and construction administration. Collaborates with the project team to organize and plan projects."}, {"h": "Responsibilities", "t": "Collaborates with project team to effectively execute structural engineering design and delivery of structural implementation documents\nMay coordinate early phase effort for determination of most appropriate structural framing system(s) and project criteria including building code, fire-rating, gravity/lateral loads and other unique requirements of the project\nPerforms effectively as a team member during design and/or construction phases\nMay prepare and/or review structural specifications for projects at each phase of delivery\nMaintains active awareness of the production schedule for responsible task(s)\nCoordinates structural CA effort including engineering site visitation, field report documentation, submittal review, response to project RFI’s, and review of structural change order requests\nRevises implementation documents from markups and/or instructions and reviews completed tasks at key intervals for accuracy/completeness\nReviews work of EIT staff\nDirects the work of structural drafting staff for implementation documentation\nUtilizes standard engineering practices and techniques to adjust and correlate data; recognizes and resolves discrepancies in results\nMay be responsible for communication with other disciplines, vendors and contractors to ensure incorporation of all information into project requirements\nParticipates in team meetings to discuss project issues, coordination with other disciplines and technical issues\nConsistently documents project meetings and telephone conversations\nMaintains knowledge of products and materials available on the market\nTravel may be required"}, {"h": "Education and Experience", "t": "Accredited professional degree in Civil, Structural or Architectural Engineering or related field\nTypically 5+ years of experience\nLicenses and Certifications\nProfessional engineering or structural engineering licensure required (structural engineering licensure preferred)\nKnowledge, Skills and Abilities\nAdvanced – expert-level experience, knowledge or skills\nIntermediate – experience, knowledge or skills required to produce high-quality solutions or work\nBasic – familiar with primary concepts or capabilities and may perform elementary functions depending on role\nIntermediate knowledge of software such as Revit and BIM required\nIntermediate knowledge of structural analytical software required\nIntermediate knowledge of MS Office Suite required\nIntermediate knowledge of building codes, material design standards, select structural standards, constructability, etc. required\nBasic knowledge of project management tools (Vision, Portfolio, etc.) preferred\nIntermediate knowledge of integrated design, engineering building systems and QA/QC process required\nIntermediate ability to communicate in a clear, concise and professional manner both verbally and in writing required\nIntermediate ability to problem solve and apply innovative solutions required\nIntermediate ability to work and collaborate in a team environment required\nIntermediate ability to work on multiple projects at the same time required\nIntermediate ability to effectively meet deadlines at expected quality required\nBase Salary Range: $84k - $105k annually - Chicago locations only.\nThe estimate displayed represents the general base salary range of candidates hired in the Chicago location only. We may ultimately pay more or less than the posted range based on the location of the role. Factors that may be used to determine your actual salary may include internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training.\nHKS offers a comprehensive total compensation & benefits package with health, dental, and vision care coverage, 401(k) plans, life & AD&D insurance, short/long term disability plans, paid days off (sick leave, parental leave, vacation), and much more for benefits-eligible employees. To learn more about our benefits visit this page.\nIf you currently work for HKS, please submit your application via the Internal Careers Portal .\nHKS is an EEO/AA Employer: M/F/Disabled/Veteran"}], "k": ["bim", "building-codes", "construction-administration", "project-management", "quality-control", "revit", "structural-analysis"], "b": ["life-insurance", "parental-leave"]}, "b68d617203": {"s": [{"h": "Overview", "t": "A recognized practitioner and licensed engineer who possesses strong technical abilities and manages implementation documentation. Uses the firm’s resources (people, processes, and tools) and assignments with proficiency, fluency and aptitude. Teaches and mentors staff and effectively embodies and expresses the firm’s values and mission."}, {"h": "Responsibilities", "t": "Coordinates structural project team efforts to facilitate effective execution of structural engineering design and the delivery of structural implementation documents\nLeads early phase effort for determination of most appropriate structural framing system(s)\nEstablishes structural project criteria including building code, fire-rating, gravity/lateral loads and unique requirements of the project\nPerforms effectively as a senior team member during design and/or construction phases\nPrepares and/or reviews structural specifications for projects at each phase of delivery\nMaintains active awareness of the production schedule for responsible project(s)\nEstablishes credibility through project management skills\nEffectively manages structural CA effort including engineering site visitation, field report documentation, submittal review, response to project RFI’s, and review of structural change order requests\nReviews implementation documents at key phases/intervals for accuracy and completeness.\nSupervises junior project team members, both engineering and drafting staff. Delegates appropriate tasks, answers questions, and holds junior project team members accountable.\nReviews staff performance relative to project contributions on a regular basis in a constructive manner to strengthen team(s)\nUtilizes standard engineering practices and techniques to adjust and correlate data; recognizes and resolves discrepancies in results\nResponsible for communication with other disciplines, clients, vendors and contractors to ensure incorporation of all information into project requirements\nParticipates in and leads team meetings to discuss project issues, coordination with other disciplines and technical issues\nConsistently documents project meetings and telephone conversations\nMaintains up to date knowledge of products and materials available on the market\nTravel will be required"}, {"h": "Education and Experience", "t": "Accredited professional degree in Civil, Structural or Architectural Engineering or related field\nTypically 7+ years of experience\nLicenses and Certifications\nProfessional engineering or structural engineering licensure required (structural engineering licensure preferred)"}, {"h": "Ability to be licensed in multiple states preferred", "t": "Knowledge, Skills and Abilities\nAdvanced – expert-level experience, knowledge or skills\nIntermediate – experience, knowledge or skills required to produce high-quality solutions or work\nBasic – familiar with primary concepts or capabilities and may perform elementary functions depending on role\nAdvanced understanding on the use of Revit and BIM in the delivery of implementation documents required\nIntermediate knowledge of MS Office Suite required\nAdvanced knowledge of building codes and material design standards required\nAdvanced knowledge in select structural systems required\nAdvanced technical knowledge through a combination of academic experience, work experience and continuing education required\nBasic knowledge of project management tools (Vision, Portfolio, etc.) preferred\nIntermediate knowledge of integrated design, engineering building systems and QA/QC process required\nAdvanced organizational skills and the ability to work on multiple projects at the same time required\nAdvanced ability to exercise judgment and discretion, set priorities and manage competing demands required\nAdvanced ability to communicate in a clear, concise and professional manner both verbally and in writing required\nAdvanced ability to problem solve and apply innovative solutions required\nAdvanced ability to work and encourage collaboration in a team environment required\nAdvanced ability to work on multiple projects at the same time required\nAdvance ability to effectively meet deadlines at expected quality required\nBase Salary Range: $99k - $141k annually - Chicago and Washington DC locations only.\nThe estimate displayed represents the general base salary range of candidates hired in the Chicago and Washington DC locations only. We may ultimately pay more or less than the posted range based on the location of the role. Factors that may be used to determine your actual salary may include internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training.\nHKS offers a comprehensive total compensation & benefits package with health, dental, and vision care coverage, 401(k) plans, life & AD&D insurance, short/long term disability plans, paid days off (sick leave, parental leave, vacation), and much more for benefits-eligible employees. To learn more about our benefits visit this page.\nIf you currently work for HKS, please submit your application via the Internal Careers Portal .\nHKS is an EEO/AA Employer: M/F/Disabled/Veteran"}], "k": ["bim", "building-codes", "project-management", "quality-control", "revit"], "b": ["certification-support", "life-insurance", "parental-leave"]}, "6ac1dde0f1": {"s": [{"h": "%PDF-1.7%����", "t": "11 0 obj endobj\nxref\n11 43\n0000000016 00000 n\n0000001414 00000 n\n0000001578 00000 n\n0000001620 00000 n\n0000002736 00000 n\n0000002761 00000 n\n0000002896 00000 n\n0000003332 00000 n\n0000003367 00000 n\n0000003480 00000 n\n0000003564 00000 n\n0000003945 00000 n\n0000004448 00000 n\n0000005418 00000 n\n0000006242 00000 n\n0000006782 00000 n\n0000006870 00000 n\n0000007372 0000