sional experience\nYou have strong powers of spatial visualization\nYou’re familiar with finite elements and CAD software\nYou speak fluent German and have a very good command of English"}, {"h": "You’re ready to take on responsibility and play an active role", "t": "Your application\n\nWe look forward to receiving your application along with your preferred starting date.\nIf you have any questions, please do not hesitate to get in touch.\n\nThe collectively agreed minimum gross salary for this position is 3.145 EUR p.m. (BG 4/1 for 40 h/Week) with a willingness to offer higher pay depending on qualifications and experience.\n\nApply Now\n\nJob Description PDF (2 MB)\n\nWerner Sobek Wien ZT GmbH\nPersonal/HR\nUngargasse 37\n1030 Vienna (AT)\nTel. +43.1.928 08 24-0\ncareer@wernersobek.com\nwww.wernersobek.com\n\nBelgrade\nBerlin\nBuenos Aires\nCopenhagen\nDubai\nFrankfurt\nHamburg\nIstanbul\nNew York\nRiyadh\nStuttgart\nTashkent\nVienna\nWeinheim"}, {"h": "About us", "t": "Services\nNews\nTopics\nFocus\nProjects\nCareer\nMedia\nNewsletter\nContact\nImprint\nPrivacy Policy\nDisclaimer\nEN\nDE\nThis button closes the dialog. Its functionality is identical to the Accept only essential cookies button.\nPrivacy Preference\n\nWe use cookies on our website. Some of them are essential, while others help us to improve this website and your experience.\n\nWe use cookies and other technologies on our website. Some of them are essential, while others help us to improve this website and your experience.\n\nPersonal data may be processed (e.g. IP addresses), for example for personalized ads and content or ad and content measurement.\n\nYou can find more information about the use of your data in our privacy policy.\n\nYou can revoke or adjust your selection at any time under Settings.\n\nThe following is a list of service groups for which consent can be given. The first service group is essential and cannot be unchecked.\nEssential\nStatistics\nExternal Media\nSave\nAccept all\nIndividual Privacy Preferences\nCookie Details\nPrivacy Policy\nImprint"}], "k": ["statistics"]}, "d17bb7e694": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Structural Engineer (m/f/x)\n\nProject Work\n\nRome\nen | it\n\nTo support our team in Rome, we are looking for a structural engineer (m/f/x), preferably registered with good English skills."}, {"h": "Your duties", "t": "Structural design processing of national and international building construction projects (calculation and/or drafting)\nCoordination with architects, clients, and contractors\nDevelopment of intelligent solutions in cooperation with architects and specialist planners\nYour profile\nGood knowledge of the English language (B2/C1). Knowledge of German or French language will be considered an added value.\nGood university theoretical knowledge related to reinforced concrete and steel structures, also in a seismic zone, according to Italian standards and Eurocodes\nSpirit of analysis and synthesis, motivation, organisational skills and autonomy in one's work.\nAbility to work in an international team with good interpersonal skills\nKnowledge of the following software: Excel, Word, Finite Element Calculation Software (basic knowledge), Autocad and/or Revit and/or Rhino (basic knowledge)\nKnowledge of parametric tools (Grasshopper, Karamba, Dynamo, etc.) is a plus"}, {"h": "What we offer", "t": "Interesting and varied tasks in an environment of innovative and unique national and international projects\nPossibility to participate in an internal Erasmus programme within the B+G Group"}, {"h": "Internal and external training and further education measures", "t": "International working environment\nA motivated design team\nCollaboration with renowned architectural firms\nFlexible working hours\nCompany mobile phone after the probationary period for professional and private use\n\nWe look forward to receiving your application.\n\nInterested candidates may submit their resume to application@bollinger-grohmann.it , indicating in the subject line: Application for Structural Engineer at B+G Rome\n\nThis position is open to candidates who consent to the processing of their personal data.\n\napply via email"}], "k": ["autocad", "concrete-design", "dynamo", "excel", "grasshopper", "revit", "rhino", "steel-design", "structural-analysis"], "r": {"lang": ["English (B2)", "German (B2)", "French (B2)"]}}, "2245c35137": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Structural Engineer (m/f/x)\n\nProject manager\n\nBudapest\nen | hu"}, {"h": "About the job", "t": "Structural design for international and national projects\nConsultation with architects, builders and contractors\nDeveloping creative structural design solutions in collaboration with architects and professional designers\nManaging a team of 3-9 people"}, {"h": "Specialised qualification (M.Sc.)", "t": "Structural designer licence\nMinimum 10 years of professional experience\nIntermediate level of English and German\nGood communication skills and team spirit\nCommitment to structural design and implementation of complex structures\nAdvantages\nKnowledge of DLUBAL, MB, ETABS programs\nInternational work experience\nIntermediate knowledge of other foreign languages\nCategory B driving licence"}, {"h": "What we offer", "t": "Stable company background, long term perspective\nAbove average salary, cafeteria, mobile phone even for private use\nFull-time registered employment\nInternational experience, participation in international projects\nOpportunity to work in our foreign office on a temporary basis\nModern working tools, pleasant office environment\nFamily-friendly management, helpful colleagues, flexible working hours\nSeveral company meetings, team-builders per year\n\nIf you are interested, please send your application with your payment request to the following e-mail address. Please enclose your CV.\n\napply via email"}], "k": ["etabs", "structural-analysis"], "b": ["flexible-hours"]}, "7ec1368fd9": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Climate Action\nProjects"}, {"h": "About Us", "t": "News & Insights\nContact\nSearch\nWork With Us\nAll\nLondon\nNottingham\nOxford\nBristol\nRemote Studio\n\nFrom the very first days of the practice, the focused desire to take care is a quality that has elevated our practice. We care for each other. We care for the people we collaborate with. We take care in our work and the projects we work on. And we care for our communities and for the environment.\n\nIn recent years, the practice has made a concerted effort to better reflect the diversity of the places we live and work in. We still have some way to go, but we have drawn considerable strength from the different cultures and different ways of thinking that this approach has brought us.\n\nEveryone that wants to contribute to great engineering is welcomed here. Maybe that’s you too?\n\nStructural Engineer with 3+ years' exprerience, Oxford\n\nDo you have 3+ years’ experience as a Structural Engineer? Interested in working on a broad range of projects? If so, we’d love to talk to you about what Price & Myers can offer for someone with your experience.\n\nThis is a full-time position based in our Oxford studio.\n\nPrice & Myers is committed to encouraging equality, diversity and inclusion among our workforce. We are an equal opportunity employer.\n\nNote\n\nPlease email a CV and cover letter to Ian Flewitt at careers@pricemyers.com.\n\nNo recruitment agents please.\n\nDownload\n\nDownload Full Job Specification\n\nStructural Engineer with 3-4 years' experience, Bristol\n\nWant to work with a friendly group of professionals committed to great engineering?\n\nWe are looking for an enthusiastic engineer with 3-4 years’ experience to join our newly established Bristol studio. You’ll need to: have a good, IStructE- or ICE-accredited degree in structural or civil engineering, be a good communicator, and have a desire to help us to continue designing great engineering.\n\nPrice & Myers is committed to encouraging equality, diversity and inclusion in our workforce. We are an equal opportunity employer.\n\nNote\n\nPlease send your CV and cover letter via email to Anna Wai: careers@pricemyers.com.\n\nNo recruitment agents please.\n\nDownload\n\nDownload Full Job Specification"}, {"h": "We're looking for Graduate Structural and Civil Engineers", "t": "Ready to start and grow your career in structural or civil engineering? If you're looking to commence employment as a graduate starting in Autumn/Winter 2026, we'd love to hear from you.\n\nWe are looking for sharp-minded, confident, sociable people who want to work on a variety of interesting, high-quality and challenging projects within our structural or civil engineering teams.\n\nPrice & Myers are committed to encouraging equality, diversity, and inclusion among our workforce. We are an equal opportunity employer.\n\nNote\n\nDownload the job description and email a CV and covering letter to Jamie Beeson using the following address: graduatejobs@pricemyers.com. No recruitment agents please.\n\nDownload\n\nDownload Full Job Specification\n\nSummer Placement\n\nSummer is closer than you think, so now is the time to start planning for your Summer Placement at Price & Myers. We have opportunities for sharp-minded students studying an engineering-relevant degree to join our structural or civil engineering teams.\n\nAre you an engineering undergraduate and looking for the right environment to build your CV and your portfolio? We’d love to hear from you.\n\nPrice & Myers is committed to encouraging equality, diversity and inclusion among our workforce. We are an equal opportunity employer.\n\nNote\n\nDownload the job description and email a CV and covering letter to Jamie Beeson using the following address: summerplacements@pricemyers.com\n\nNo recruitment agents please.\n\nDownload\n\nDownload Full Job Specification\n\n© Price & Myers 2026\n\nPolicies\n\nSite by Stylo"}], "k": [], "r": {"exp": 3}}, "cf4f97a058": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Plant (ACP) in Piketon, Ohio. Centrus Energy is seeking an experienced, proactive Civil /Structural Design Engineer to lead... from design to turnover. What You Will Do: Lead Structural Design & Analysis: Drive civil /structural engineering for site"}], "k": ["structural-analysis"]}, "d2b1462163": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...Number: 189653Apply: JobOptimized Process Designs, LLC (OPD), a Koch Engineered Solutions company, is seeking to add a Structural Engineer to join their growing team. In this role, you will support the civil and structural design of EPC projects from early development..."}], "k": ["structural-analysis"]}, "592bd1fe10": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "About Exponent\nExponent is the only premium engineering and scientific consulting firm with the depth and breadth of expertise to solve... ...Offices globally\nOur Opportunity\nWe are currently seeking a Civil/ Structural Engineer for our Civil & Structural Engineering..."}], "k": []}, "4dc79a3c66": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "OverviewAs a civil/ structural engineer at MPR, you will serve as both an engineer and project leader, applying civil/structural engineering expertise to solve complex challenges while managing project scope, schedule, budget, and client relationships. Consulting means no..."}], "k": ["account-management"]}, "c4ddc34ae6": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...how you could help make great things possible not only in your community, but around the world. HDR is looking for a Senior Structural Engineer to join our team in Raleigh or Charlotte. This individual will be responsible for the structural design of facilities in support..."}], "k": ["structural-analysis"]}, "8533918cc2": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "DescriptionThe Staff Civil/ Structural Engineer will be a key member of project teams, responsible for creating world-class designs for new projects, alterations and redevelopments on a variety of projects with a focus on marine structures, including piers, wharfs, bulkheads..."}], "k": []}, "023bc7749e": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...Designing and detailing mat and pier type foundations for substation structures, the Remote Civil Structural Engineer will ensure quality and compliance while managing project costs and adhering to client requirements."}, {"h": "Key responsibilities", "t": "Design and detail foundations..."}], "k": ["detailing"]}, "c1c74ea03c": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...PermanentWorking pattern: Full time / Flexible workingIndustry: Engineering / CPStructural EngineeringCompany: HaysConsultant: Oliver... ...through sustainable energy systems.What You’ll DoAs a Principal Civil & Structural Engineer, you’ll take technical ownership of complex..."}], "k": []}, "2fdb515c14": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "GFT is seeking a talented Principal Civil / Structural Engineer to join our team in our Roseville, CA. This role follows a hybrid work model, requiring regular attendance at our Roseville office.Our specialists have the in-depth knowledge to excel on the most challenging..."}], "k": ["excel"]}, "c7d1858f7d": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...that provides design support for large and small-scale substation engineering projects. This is an excellent growth opportunity for a self-... ...to learn and take on new challenges. In the role of Substation Civil - Structural Engineer, we'll count on you to:Lead, oversee,..."}], "k": []}, "411989af39": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "... Civil/ Structural Engineer\nClient has a position available for an early career Civil/Structural Engineer to support our growing Energy practice Engineering Center of Excellence. For this role, client offers the freedom and flexibility to work in a hybrid office/remote..."}], "k": []}, "dcf943429a": {"s": [{"h": "A WORLD LEADER IN TESTING, INSPECTION & CERTIFICATION SERVICES", "t": "Bureau Veritas offers dynamic, exciting employment opportunities with an attractive salary/benefit package and an opportunity to play a vital role with a global organization. If you would enjoy working in a dynamic environment and are looking for an opportunity to become part of a stellar team of professionals, we invite you to apply online today.\nBureau Veritas is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and as such we recruit, hire, train, and promote persons in all job classifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, age, marital status, citizen status, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetics, status as a protected veteran, or any other non-job-related characteristics.\nThis position is responsible to ensure equal opportunity in employment in that all persons are treated equally and on the basis of merit, in decisions regarding selection, placement, promotions, training, work assignments, transfers and other personnel actions.\nCity: Remote\nState: Remote"}, {"h": "Summary", "t": "The Senior Civil/Structural/Geotechnical Engineer will be part of the BV owner’s engineering and technical advisory group; a multi-discipline team focus on servicing clients in the renewable power and electric utilities industry.\nOwner’s Engineering services cover the whole CAPEX cycle of the project (conceptual/feasibility, permitting support, detailed design review, equipment inspection, construction support, commissioning and startup support).\nThis position requires both significant technical expertise in Civil/Structural/Geotechnical engineering and experience in the design and construction of renewable power generation, as well as a client-oriented approach to ensure that the required quality level (against applicable industry codes and standards, project technical specific requirements, and owner’s specifications) is met while simultaneously minimizing the risks on the project schedule and cost for our clients.\nThe candidate will be responsible to perform design reviews following the BV typical design review process focusing on the following objectives (including but not limited to):\nDesign meets all specified permitting and contractual requirements (owner’s requirements, interconnection / interface requirements, etc.) and is in compliance with applicable codes, standards and local permit conditions.\n\n· Design includes the strategy for confirming and demonstrating that performance requirements can be met\n\n· Design drawings, codes and specification are full and complete and accurately represent the completed project\n\n· Equipment project ancillary facilities are used within their specified performance envelope and will meet the project expected design life and performance level.\n\n· Cost optimization, constructability and practicability after considering all project requirements\n\n· Scheduling considerations including identification of long lead items and sequencing of construction are taken into account\nThe selected candidate should have a strong Civil/Structural/Geotechnical engineering and renewables project development, design and construction experience background (utility-scale solar, wind, battery storage, and combined generation projects)."}, {"h": "Responsibilities", "t": "The candidate will be responsible to perform design reviews following BV typical design review process outlined below:\n\n· Receive design documents and make a review plan\n\n· Verify / Confirm the applicable Codes / Standards / Requirements applicable to the project\n\n· Review the project design for constructability and practicality.\n\n· Check the authenticity and completeness of the document\n\n· Perform design review against the applicable codes / standards and owner’s requirements. At the completion of review, each drawing is given an approval status. During design review, attention shall be given to such aspects as: proper input data and modeling, adequate selection of design parameters and design conditions, any nonconformance to contractual requirements that imposes risks on the project schedule and cost will be immediately brought up to Client’s attention.\n\n· Develop and issue review comment report / log to Client"}, {"h": "Job Requirements", "t": "Working knowledge of Civil/Structural/Geotechnical engineering theories and principles\n\n· Minimum 10 years of experience as a Civil/Structural engineer working on all aspects of the development, design and construction of renewable power and other related utility projects\n\n· Familiarity with applicable Civil/Structural design and performance standards and procedures and other related standards is required\n\n· Ability to interpret codes, standards, regulations, and practices and assess their applicability to Client’s project.\n\n· Ability to review technical geotechnical, hydrology, and other similar reports and assess and communicate project conformance with the reports with the client.\n\n· Familiarity with US health and safety standards as applicable to renewable energy projects is desirable.\n\n· Proficient with Microsoft office applications and strong computer skills\n\n· Experience with dynamic modeling software packages is strongly preferred\n\n· Strong oral and written communication skills that foster positive interpersonal communication\n\n· Self-motivated individual capable of working independently with minimal oversight and in a fast-paced team environment\n\n· Strong time management skills with ability to independently plan and organize work\n\n· Ability to prioritize tasks and participate on multiple projects simultaneously in a fast-paced setting\n\n· Critical thinking, attention to detail, effective in high stress situations, flexible, dependable, honest, and ethical\n\n· A mix of field engineering, EOR, OE, and EPC experience in renewable energy is highly desirable\n\n· A good background mix of civil, geotechnical, hydrological and structural engineering is also highly desirable"}, {"h": "Education / Certification Requirements", "t": "· Possessing a 4-year Civil engineering degree is required\n\n· Currently holds or has previously held a valid US Professional Engineer license is required\nIf you are an individual with a disability and you would like us to assist you with searching the Careers Page site for employment opportunities and/or assistance with completing your profile and application, please contact us at 1-888-357-7020 or email us with your request to .\nWe are happy to assist you and encourage you to consider Bureau Veritas for your next great career opportunity!\nIf you would like additional information regarding Bureau Veritas ' federal obligations in regards to equal employment opportunity, please click the link below:\nOriginally posted on Himalayas"}], "k": ["scheduling", "structural-analysis"], "r": {"exp": 10}}, "d5d508fd22": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...honesty and operate ethically in everything you do.\nJob Description\nWe are looking for an experienced and driven Civil/ Structural Engineer with a wealth of industry knowledge. The ideal candidate will have a strong background and interest in Structural and or..."}], "k": []}, "98f183df35": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...We're hiring a Civil/ Structural Engineer to support industrial facility projects across the Pacific Northwest, with a strong focus on seismic design, steel and concrete structures, and facility upgrades.\nThis is a mid-level role (5-8 years experience) ideal for an engineer..."}], "k": ["seismic-design"], "r": {"exp": 5}}, "abffe5f841": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "We are recruiting on purpose a Civil Structural Engineer in Nashville, TN.This is the Coolest Structural Engineering Job doing Building Design in Nashville!!!Fantastic client listed as one of the Best Structural Engineering firms to work for over the past 10 years running..."}], "k": []}, "b345ab3e43": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...innovation in sustainable infrastructure and our expertise in engineering, procurement, consulting and construction, together we are building... ...selected) which may include any/all of the following: criminal/ civil background check, drug screen, and motor vehicle records search..."}], "k": ["procurement"]}, "28c3c38c67": {"s": [{"h": null, "t"