t 10 years running..."}], "k": []}, "cdb74b7988": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Job Description"}, {"h": "Job ID#", "t": "5622"}, {"h": "Position Type", "t": "Permanent or Contract"}, {"h": "Duration", "t": "Temp/Direct"}, {"h": "Positions Available... ...", "t": "3Technical Solutions Inc. is currently seeking a Senior Structural Engineer, for our client in the Pittsburgh, PA areaPosition..."}], "k": []}, "a08509c718": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Weston & Sampson is seeking a Senior Structural Engineer to work alongside our growing team in Rocky Hill, CT.What you’ll do:Perform on-site field work related to buildings and other structuresWork with others to plan, design, and perform construction administration of..."}], "k": ["construction-administration"]}, "1eb91db58e": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Senior Structural Engineer/ DesignerOur client is a highly regarded, established and growing structural design and engineering firm. They offer an outstanding work culture and work/life balance and are strongly committed to employee growth, job satisfaction and continual..."}], "k": ["structural-analysis"]}, "ffa5b3b8a1": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...VA or Washington, DC office is now hiring for a Senior Bridge Engineer to support our Bridge projects in Virginia/DC region, with a desire... ...execution. In this role, you will plan and design Bridge structures to ensure structural reliability, resource efficiency and cost..."}], "k": []}, "f7d7f1f3b6": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Structural Engineer Hemel Hempstead £Negotiable Would you like to work for consultancy who provide multi...-disciplinary services in areas including Structural and Civil Engineering, Building Surveying, Land Surveying, Transport"}], "k": []}, "eb8f2c34ca": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Description: Joining Sargent & Lundy's Nuclear Power Group as a Structural Engineer presents a distinctive... U.S. for this position. Essential skills and experience: BS degree in Civil Engineering with an emphasis in Structural Engineering"}], "k": []}, "5533d0684d": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "STRUCTURAL TECHNOLOGIES develops and integrates products, engineering support, repair and maintenance services to provide value-added solutions to owners, engineers and contractors.\n\nWe provide specialty contracting services through our contracting companies, and state-of-the-art proprietary products and engineering support services through our technologies company.\n\nWith over 2,500 employees working from locations nationwide and in select international markets, we serve the Commercial, Public, Transportation Industrial, and Power markets to tackle the toughest construction challenges. STRUCTURAL TECHNOLOGIES is the in-house engineering business line of Structural Group.\nSenior Structural Engineer – STRUCTURAL TECHNOLOGIES\nAre you a structural engineer who thrives on solving complex challenges? At STRUCTURAL TECHNOLOGIES , you’ll design and deliver solutions that keep critical infrastructure strong and safe. Join our team and make an impact on industrial and power generation projects across North America. A successful candidate can be located anywhere in the United States near a major airport.\nWho We Are\nAt STRUCTURAL TECHNOLOGIES we’re problem solvers, collaborators, and innovators. Together with our sister companies, STRUCTURAL, PULLMAN, and VECTOR CONSTRUCTION, we form the largest concrete repair and maintenance provider in the United States . Our integrated teams investigate, design, and build solutions for clients in the industrial and power generation verticals. If you love tackling tough challenges and working with passionate people, you’ll fit right in."}, {"h": "What You’ll Do", "t": "As a Senior Structural Engineer with a construction support focus, you’ll work closely with our operations branches, supporting repair projects. Potential projects include equipment foundations, environmental (liquid-retaining) containment, storage facilities, chimneys, and cooling towers."}, {"h": "Key Responsibilities", "t": "Oversee structural engineering construction support services as the primary point of contact\nReview engineering deliverables including drawings, specifications, and written reports\nRespond to changed conditions in the field and lead design updates\nDesign and analyze temporary structures using relevant industry standards.\nPrepare and review calculations and sketches using hand and software methods\nCollaborate closely with construction teams to integrate structural repair solutions effectively\nPerform site visits and inspections to assess structural conditions and oversee repairs.\nMentor junior engineers and technicians."}, {"h": "Qualifications", "t": "Bachelor’s degree in civil/structural engineering\nLicensed Professional Engineer (PE)\n8+ years of relevant structural engineering and construction experience\nEligible to obtain a TWIC and site access badges for industrial and power facilities\nWillingness to travel for site visits – maximum 50% of time; typical trip lengths of 2-10 days\nStrong technical writing and verbal communication skills\nTechnical accuracy and attention to detail in design\nA love for solving problems and understanding how things work"}, {"h": "Preferred Skills & Certifications", "t": "Advanced degree in civil or structural engineering\nLicensed Structural Engineer (SE)\nKnowledge of concrete degradation mechanisms\nExperience with repairs to existing structures\nFamiliar with relevant codes and standards such as ACI, ICRI, AISC, AWS\nExperience with structural steel analysis, including bolted and welded connections\nKnowledge of OSHA 1926.451 fall protection standards for scaffolding and rigging\nExperience with Finite Element Analysis Software (ANSYS, SAP2000, Staad.Pro, or equivalent)\nExperience with AutoCAD, Revit, or other BIM software\nActive in professional organizations, such as ASCE, ACI, AMPP, SEI, ICRI\nEnthusiasm for teamwork and continuous learning\nReady to Build Something Amazing?\nOur ideal candidate is a positively focused professional with a desire to grow while supporting industry-leading repairs. This role will directly impact business performance by focusing on safety, reducing rework, and improving field outcomes.\nSTRUCTURAL TECHNOLOGIES has a proud company culture that promotes 24/7 safety, quality, and collaborative teamwork. We strive to create a workplace that is inclusive, caring, and enjoyable, where every team member can thrive, grow, and find satisfaction in their work.\n\nOur mission is to make structures stronger and last longer, but we are equally committed to providing a safe and enriching experience for our people. We offer competitive compensation and benefits including medical and dental insurance, 401(k), paid holidays & vacation, tuition reimbursement, career development and growth opportunities."}, {"h": "EOE/M/F/D/V", "t": "Due to the nature of the client facilities this role will be required to gain entry to, we are unable to provide employment visa sponsorship for this position\nStructural Technologies is proud of a company culture that promotes 24/7 safety and quality. EOE/M/F/D/V\nOriginally posted on Himalayas"}], "k": ["autocad", "aws", "bim", "etabs", "fea", "hr-operations", "osha-safety", "preventive-maintenance", "revit", "safety", "steel-design", "technical-writing"], "b": ["dental", "generous-pto", "tuition"]}, "7c454eded7": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "About Us:BW Design Group is a fully integrated architecture, engineering, construction, system integration, and consulting firm committed... ...own success and fulfillment.When you join Design Group as a Structural Engineer, you are joining a team that will challenge you and..."}], "k": ["supply-chain"]}, "af530d39de": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Skip To Job Description"}, {"h": "VIEW OUR WEBSITE", "t": "Entry Level Structural Engineer - Structural Designer\nLos Angeles, CA\nFull Time\nLos Angeles Office\nEntry Level"}, {"h": "SHARE", "t": "🌟 Launch Your Engineering Career at Holmes US! 🚀\n\nAre you a recent graduate or new professional ready to make your mark in structural engineering? We're seeking passionate Structural Designers to join our innovative team and start an exciting journey in shaping the built environment!\n\nWho We Are: We're Holmes US - an international design firm where engineering meets innovation! With offices across the West Coast and roots in New Zealand, we're known for pushing boundaries and asking \"why not?\" when others say \"impossible.\""}, {"h": "Your Journey as a Structural Designer", "t": "Design and analyze structural elements for diverse projects\nCreate detailed structural drawings and specifications\nUse cutting-edge design software\nVisit project sites for hands-on experience\nLearn from industry experts\nMaybe even pick up some Māori words from our Kiwi colleagues!"}, {"h": "B.S. in Structural Engineering (M.S. preferred)", "t": "1+ years of experience (internships count!)\nEagerness to learn and grow\nStrong communication skills\nTechnical curiosity and creativity\nTeam player mindset"}, {"h": "Why You'll Love It Here", "t": "🌟 Learning & Growth\n\nPersonalized mentorship program\nInteractive technical training via Holmes University\nAccess to specialized material committees\nGlobal knowledge sharing opportunities\nClear career progression path\n\n💪 Real World Impact\n\nWork on exciting, diverse projects\nLearn from industry leaders\nContribute to sustainable design\nMake a difference in your community\n\n🎯 The Good Stuff\n\nFlexible hybrid work environment"}, {"h": "Comprehensive benefits (including pet insurance!)", "t": "Genuine work-life balance\nCollaborative, supportive culture\nRegular team events and activities"}, {"h": "Depending on your employment status, benefits may include", "t": "Hybrid work model (in office Tues, Wed, Thurs)\nComprehensive Medical, Dental, Vision, Life, AD&D, Short-term and Long-term Disability and other voluntary plans\nFlexible Spending Accounts for Medical & Childcare\nHealth Savings Account\nPet Insurance\nEmployee Assistance Program\nPaid Time off - Vacation, Sick, Personal Leave, Family Leave for new parents, and Community Service time\nPaid Holidays\nPre-Tax Commuter Transit\n401(k) retirement savings with Company contribution\nCompany sponsored events\nDiversity / Inclusion programs and initiatives\n\nCompensation: Estimated at $76,000 - $88,500 + biannual profit share bonus potential. Salary will be commensurate with experience / skills and location.\n\nOur Commitment: At Holmes, we believe in building teams as diverse as the communities we serve. We provide equal support and opportunities for all our people to thrive, grow, and develop. Dream big - we'll help you get there!\n\nReady to join a team that believes in pushing boundaries and having fun while doing it? Apply now and be part of our next chapter of engineering excellence! 🏗️\n\nP.S. - Did we mention we have great snacks in the office? Because we totally do. 🍪\n\n#LI-hybrid\n\nApply for this position"}, {"h": "REQUIRED*", "t": "First Name*\nLast Name*\nEmail Address*\nPhone*\nAddress\nResume*\nAttach resume or Paste resume\nCover Letter\nAre you legally authorized to work in the United States?*\n-- No answer --\nYes\nNo\nDo you now or in the future require visa sponsorship to continue working in the United States?*\n-- No answer --\nYes\nNo\nWere you referred by a current Holmes employee?\n-- No answer --\nYes\nNo\nIf referred, please indicate the name of the employee.\nThe following questions are entirely optional.\nTo comply with government Equal Employment Opportunity and/or Affirmative Action reporting regulations, we are requesting (but NOT requiring) that you enter this personal data. This information will not be used in connection with any employment decisions, and will be used solely as permitted by state and federal law. Your voluntary cooperation would be appreciated. Learn more.\nGender\nDecline to answer\nFemale\nMale\nRace/Ethnicity\nDecline to answer\nHispanic or Latino\nWhite, not Hispanic or Latino\nBlack or African-American, not Hispanic or Latino\nAsian, not Hispanic or Latino\nNative Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander, not Hispanic or Latino\nAmerican Indian or Alaskan Native, not Hispanic or Latino\nTwo or More Races, not Hispanic or Latino\nMENA (Middle Eastern and North African)\nHuman Check*"}, {"h": "SUBMIT APPLICATION", "t": "This website uses cookies and other analytics technologies.\nBy selecting \"Allow\", you consent to the recording, use and sharing of your website activity by this website and its service providers."}], "k": ["data-analysis", "sustainability"], "b": ["bonus", "generous-pto", "life-insurance", "visa-sponsorship"]}, "3dc5dacb42": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Structural Engineer South London Permanent £36,000 - £52,000 Are you a structural design engineer with experience... under the guidance of a chartered structural engineer with a view to developing your client and architect liaison skills"}], "k": ["structural-analysis"]}, "12c574351c": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Job description: You’re a Structural Engineer ready to take on more responsibility—leading projects, developing... with Civil , MEP, Environmental, Energy and Water teams, giving you the opportunity to contribute to projects in a more integrated"}], "k": ["mep"]}, "6231bc052c": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Structural Design Engineer Permanent Liverpool £35,000 - £45,000 This Multi-disciplinary Engineering Consultancy... have a requirement for a Structural Design Engineer to join their building structures team as they continue to expand due to a large"}], "k": ["structural-analysis"]}, "078789e48b": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": ", for all of us. Role Description As a Senior Structures Engineer , you will apply your expertise in structural sizing, analysis and finite...Job Title Senior Structures Engineer Job Location Warton – On site – We offer a range of hybrid and flexible working"}], "k": []}, "63cb8a264e": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...