s. This will help ensure candidates who share Zoox’s values apply. Highlight the broader impact of the team and Zoox. Quality applicants are drawn to work that is meaningful. How will a candidate be contributing and making a difference? Communicate that there are opportunities for learning and growth. Great candidates seek out companies that support growth and learning.\n\nRemember: Candidates are looking for cues about whether or not they will fit in at Zoox, so make sure your language is balanced and inclusive."}, {"h": "Example", "t": "The Autonomous Driving Software Integration team at Zoox is responsible for bringing together the computer science world with the automotive world in order to create an amazing product for everyone. Our team has a collaborative culture marked by openness and supportive risk-taking. You’ll be part of a passionate team dedicated to making cities safer, smarter and more sustainable.\n\nTogether with the team, you will define the driving experience of the robot by engineering application software responsible for decision making, trajectory planning, and controls.\n\nWe are looking for an engineer who is excited to traverse the autonomous driving compute stack, loves to learn new things, and likes to take ownership of major software components. If you like to work close to the robot platform and enjoy experiencing your developed software in the robot, we would like to hear from you."}, {"h": "TAGS", "t": "· Data Science\n· Communications\n· Design and Product\n· Operations\n· Finance\n· Procurement\n· Hardware Engineering\n· Product Security\n· Human Resources\n· Program Management\n· Information Technology\n· Quality\n· Legal and Policy\n· Software Engineering\n· Manufacturing Operations\n· Supply Chain\n· Systems and Safety"}, {"h": "In this role, you will", "t": "Conceptualize, design (2D and 3D), and lead development/release of vehicle body components/assemblies to meet cost, weight, performance requirements\nDevelop short and long term schedule/plans for component development, release, delivery, and validation\nDefine/negotiate requirements and specifications for body systems to achieve best in class performance in structural, NVH, and crash performance; including DFMEAs, DVP’s and PVP’s, APQP\nSupport validation testing for component/vehicle\nSupport material and manufacturing process decisions both internally and externally\nWork cross functionally and collaborate with peers, styling studio, packaging, CAE/attribute/test teams, management, manufacturing, suppliers\nDevelop processes, procedures and best practices for Body design and development"}, {"h": "Qualifications", "t": "B.S. in mechanical engineering equivalent or higher\n4+ years experience in automotive body system design/engineering (OEM/supplier, university SAE team, or equivalent)\nKnowledge/experience in vehicle engineering, automotive body systems design and engineering fundamentals, body materials and manufacturing processes, and component delivery\nExperience with the development of specifications, DFMEAs, DVP’s and PVP’s, APQP and other technical and quality assurance processes\nExperience in engineering best practices including design for six sigma (DFSS)\nAbility to implement GD&T and dimensional engineering principles in design\nProficiency with CATIA V5 or V6 CAD software\nStrong communication/collaboration skills with peers, suppliers, manufacturing, management"}, {"h": "Bonus Qualifications", "t": "Experience at automotive OEM\nKnowledge of automotive development/release process\nPolarion, Jira, and Confluence experience."}], "k": ["cad-mechanical", "gd-t", "jira", "lean-six-sigma", "procurement", "program-management", "qa-testing", "supply-chain", "system-design"], "r": {"exp": 4}}, "50ef13e4ac": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...Position Title: Principal Civil/ Structural Engineer\nLocation: Houston, TX\nGulf Companies has served the global energy industry since 1953 by supporting the complete project lifecycle and develo